# Spark ops routines (run from this VM; reach the Spark over SSH).
# Install (append-only):  ops/install-cron.sh
# Alerts: each script exits nonzero + prints on anomaly. Delivery:
#   - PUSHOVER (primary, wired 2026-07-17): ops/_common.sh resolves the Pushover
#     app token + user key from Bitwarden at runtime (items PUSHOVER_APP_TOKEN /
#     PUSHOVER_USER_KEY, BWS token from ~/.config/claude-env.sh). No secrets on
#     disk, nothing to set here. Delivery failures are logged as ALERT-DELIVERY-
#     FAILED in ~/spark-ops-logs/<routine>.log. Overrides: ops/spark-ops.env.example.
#   - MAILTO (optional): requires a working mailer (msmtp/sendmail) on this host.
MAILTO=""
# Times below are UTC, pinned by CRON_TZ. Plain cron interprets them in the
# system timezone (America/New_York on this VM), which fired these 4 h late;
# CRON_TZ makes the documented UTC schedule authoritative (fixed 2026-07-16).
CRON_TZ=UTC

# Daily liveness + error check (13:05 UTC) — quiet unless something is wrong.
5 13 * * *   /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/spark-healthcheck.sh
# Weekly NON-DISRUPTIVE inference smoke / perf-drift (Mon 13:30 UTC).
30 13 * * 1  /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/spark-smoke.sh
# Weekly security posture (Mon 14:00 UTC).
0 14 * * 1   /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/spark-security.sh
# Weekly LLM config audit (Tue 02:00 UTC). Headless `claude -p` verified 2026-06-30 (runs with bypassPermissions).
0 2 * * 2  /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/spark-audit-cron.sh
# Weekly LLM landscape recon (Sat 13:00 UTC). Headless `claude -p` spark-recon skill; commits its own LAB_NOTEBOOK entry.
0 13 * * 6  /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/spark-recon-cron.sh
# Weekly Jetson landscape recon (Sat 14:00 UTC). NOTE: this script lives here (spark/ops) but
# operates entirely against ~/dev/personal/jetson/ — see the placement comment atop the script
# for why (no jetson/ops/ tree exists yet; not worth scaffolding one for a single job).
0 14 * * 6  /home/davistroy/dev/personal/spark/ops/jetson-recon-cron.sh
